Z||000022||DreXteR||08-20-2001||12:11 AM||||Fierowrecker - I already have a set of Forger pistons and arent exacly cheaper, thats why I will keep the 2.8. Anyway doing a 3.8 sc isnt a very easy swap after all.<BR> <P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000023||Wannabe||08-20-2001||09:28 AM||||Drex, I suggest you speak with a few different camshaft suppliers and people who  have built built engines like this. I can only provide you with some general guidelines to point you in the right direction. As far as 1.5 or 1.6 rockers, if the cam is alreedy suited to a turbo application, stick with 1.5. If you use a mild cam like a Crane 2030 ro the stock cam, the extra lift with 1.6 should work well with the turbo and you will be able to check clearance since you are building the bottom end, so that may be a good way to go. See if you can check with Dennis Lagrua. I believe he had a custom grind done for his turbo 3.4.||||reg||1
